{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.KnotFactorBorromeanComposite","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.KnotFactorBorromeanComposite","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorAmphicheiral"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean_trivial_of_zero_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean_trivial_of_zero_weight","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L108-L118","doc":"**At zero alternating weight the composite is `1` and carries no\ninformation about `h`.** This is the degenerate case the upstream docstring\nnames, propagated to the composite: `w_alt = 0` makes every component `1`,\nso the `k`-fold product is `1` for every `h` and every `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.amphicheiral_factor_eq_displayed_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.amphicheiral_factor_eq_displayed_iff","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L100-L106","doc":"**The two per-component forms agree exactly on one locus.** Not a\nrearrangement of each other, and not generically equal: the derived and the\ndisplayed factor coincide iff the alternating block carries weight\n`h²/(1 + h²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean_amphicheiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean_amphicheiral","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L90-L98","doc":"**The same composite in the form the upstream corollary proves.** With each\ncomponent at `1 - w_alt(1 + h²)` — what `knot_factor_amphicheiral` derives —\nthe composite is that quantity to the `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L75-L88","doc":"**Corollary (Borromean-k composite knot factor).**\n\nA `k`-fold Brunnian composite whose components each have knot factor\n`1 - h²` has total knot factor `(1 - h²)^k`.\n\nThe per-component value is a *hypothesis* here, not an import: see the\nmodule header — `knot_factor_amphicheiral` derives `1 - w_alt(1 + h²)`\nunder the normalisation it states. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:knot-factor-borromean-composite","label":"cor:knot-factor-borromean-composite","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean_of_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_borromean_of_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L66-L73","doc":"**Uniform components give the `k`-th power.** Derived from decoupling by\n`Finset.prod_const`; the exponent is the component count, not an assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BrunnianDecoupling.decouples","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BrunnianDecoupling.decouples","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BrunnianDecoupling.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BrunnianDecoupling.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BrunnianDecoupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BrunnianDecoupling","kind":"structure","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite.lean#L57-L64","doc":"**Brunnian decoupling hypothesis.**\n\nThe knot factor of a `k`-component Brunnian composite is the product of its\ncomponents' factors — one factor per component, no cross-term. This is the\ndecoupling; it does not presuppose that the components agree. ","signatureChunk":0}]}